WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.002 --> 00:00:03.402
(drums tapping)

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:07.207
- I think a lot of people look
at hula as just women dancing

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.324
but, um, we love it, man.

00:00:09.324 --> 00:00:12.560
(drum tapping)

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.893
Hula is a story.

00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:18.318
To tell the story the way
the ancient Hawaiians did,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.378
you really need to put
yourself in that dance.

00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:22.878
You need to live like them.

00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:24.136
You need to chant like them.

00:00:24.136 --> 00:00:25.835
(chanting in Hawaiian)

00:00:25.835 --> 00:00:28.739
You need to train like them.

00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:31.572
Basically you need to become them.

00:00:33.769 --> 00:00:35.819
(drums tapping)

00:00:35.819 --> 00:00:38.476
(singer chanting)

00:00:38.476 --> 00:00:40.257
Halau is a hula school.

00:00:40.257 --> 00:00:42.557
We perform all over the world.

00:00:42.557 --> 00:00:44.809
(chanting in Hawaiian)

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:47.609
In ancient times, warriors
were actually recruited

00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:48.859
from the halau.

00:00:50.028 --> 00:00:51.708
The chief would come to look

00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:55.637
and from the ranks of the
advanced male dancers,

00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:57.769
warriors were selected.

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:01.936
The philosophy of our halau
is to kind of replicate that.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.636
- For male hula, we're basically
telling warrior stories.

00:01:06.636 --> 00:01:08.100
And to dance like a warrior,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.968
you need to train like a warrior.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.849
(waves splashing)

00:01:12.849 --> 00:01:15.940
We train in a private piece of
land on the west side of Oahu

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.249
using only what ancient Hawaiians had.

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:22.582
Whether it's rocks, the sand, the ocean.

00:01:24.089 --> 00:01:28.369
When we come to practice,
we expect to die.

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:31.329
It's strenuous on the legs, but
it's also to train your mind.

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:33.310
I tell myself and the rest of the boys,

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.060
“If I fall, it's because
my body just gave out.”

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.390
One of the hardest workouts we do

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.129
would be climbing the coconut tree.

00:01:43.129 --> 00:01:44.798
Sometimes you reach the top
and your legs are shaking

00:01:44.798 --> 00:01:46.909
because, you know, you're
holding your weight.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:49.838
And to look down knowing
that nothing's holding you

00:01:49.838 --> 00:01:51.596
you've got to kind of
have this warrior mindset

00:01:51.596 --> 00:01:53.657
as like, you know, that this is
what I want, you know.

00:01:53.657 --> 00:01:55.490
I'm going to get this.

00:02:00.468 --> 00:02:02.929
- You know, when these
gentlemen come to hula,

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:06.140
they are like a ball of clay.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.289
As kumu, I look at it as my responsibility

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:13.030
to shape them into better individuals,

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.780
better fathers, better
sons, better brothers.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.209
Our goal is that when
these men are done dancing

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:24.126
that they leave here better people.

00:02:26.851 --> 00:02:29.072
(waves splashing)

00:02:29.072 --> 00:02:30.702
- What hula does for me culturally,

00:02:30.702 --> 00:02:34.713
it still takes me back
to how Hawaii used to be.

00:02:34.713 --> 00:02:37.222
People sometimes are losing
that aloha for each other,

00:02:37.222 --> 00:02:40.502
that love for each other
and hula just gives you

00:02:40.502 --> 00:02:42.502
that reality check, man.

00:02:45.713 --> 00:02:49.302
I'm dancing until my kneecaps fall off.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.211
And even after that

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:53.844
I'm going to do whatever
I can for the halau.

00:02:53.844 --> 00:02:55.029
You know, we have this brotherhood

00:02:55.029 --> 00:02:57.825
where we take care of each other.

00:02:57.825 --> 00:02:59.934
We help push each other.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.395
It's my passion and I look forward

00:03:01.395 --> 00:03:04.562
to seeing where hula takes me in life.

